hi this is pressed I worker and today  I'm going to explain why 2% milk is  really 34 percent fat we'll start by  taking a look at the nutrition label for  milk  the name 2% milk refers to a measure of  milk fat by weight this is calculated by  taking the total weight of fat and  dividing it by the total weight of food  so we know that 2% milk is 2 percent  milk fat by weight but that's not the  relevant measure for dieters most people  are curious how much of this fat does it  contribute to my daily total by that  measure the 5 grams of fat are actually  8 percent fat by daily value a final  measure is that most dieters care about  calories and they want to know what  percentage of the calories are coming  from fat what happens when we take a  look at this measure 2% milk has 42  calories from fat and it has 125  calories surprisingly we find out that  2% milk is actually 34% fat by calories  now you may wonder why 2% milk goes by  the name of 2 percent milk fat by weight  rather than the 8 percent fat by daily  values or the 34 percent of fat by  calories and just saying this out loud  makes you realize that the number which  was picked was the lowest one it sounds  a lot better to call it 2% milk than to  call it 34 percent fat this is a game  that other food products use as well  hebrew national beef franks advertises  that it's 97% fat-free and that's  because it's true that only that it's  only 3% fat by weight when you look at  the percentage of fat by calories it's  actually 25% and this somewhat makes  sense that you wouldn't necessarily  think that beef franks  are low fat food  other food items also claim that their  very high percentage of fat-free and  again they're true because it's fat-free  by weight but not fat-free as a  percentage of calories so there's a game  theory lesson here which is that foods  that advertise health claims are  signaling that they are not necessarily  enough that they could survive without  these claims  so the counterpoint is that if you want  to look for foods which are actually  fat-free you're going to want to look  for foods which don't advertise at all  and that means you should probably stick  to fruits and vegetables thanks for  watching and please subscribe you can  follow me on my blog bind your decisions  or on Twitter at pressure Walker and get  my ebooks at Amazon
 

